From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] vcgfx: retire the boot display before taking the
 hardware

This machine now boots with a DDRV_BootMode framebuffer driver in the
kickstart and this one arriving from DEVS:Monitors, which is how AROS
expects display drivers to be installed. What it did not do was finish
the arrangement: graphics.library offers an incoming native driver the
handover interface so it can retire whatever is still writing to the
hardware, and this driver never looked at DDRVA_Handover.

The result was two owners of one display. fbgfx stayed registered and
kept refreshing its 640x480 16bpp bitmap into the firmware's framebuffer
while this driver programmed a 32bpp mode of its own over the top, and
the boot presentation kept its clock running on the old geometry. On
screen that was the desktop drawn twice and the splash smeared twice
across the width -- neither a rendering bug, both the same missing
handshake.

The interface is only valid inside New(), where graphics.library holds
the display database on the driver's behalf, so it is used there and not
kept. workbench/hidds/nouveau does the same thing for the same reason.

No DisplayRange list is passed. Ranges exist so a boot driver serving a
second, unrelated card survives the arrival of a driver for the first;
there is one display on a Pi, and a NULL list means "assume it
conflicts", which is the truth here rather than a shortcut.

diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vcgfx/vcgfx_hiddclass.c b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vcgfx/vcgfx_hiddclass.c
index 257f3da5e7..3460be2d6c 100644
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vcgfx/vcgfx_hiddclass.c
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/hidd/vcgfx/vcgfx_hiddclass.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <graphics/view.h>
 #include <hardware/custom.h>
 #include <hidd/hidd.h>
+#include <graphics/driver.h>
 #include <hidd/gfx.h>
 #include <hidd/gallium.h>
 #include <oop/oop.h>
@@ -157,6 +158,49 @@ OOP_Object *MNAME_ROOT(New)(OOP_Class *cl, OOP_Object *o, struct pRoot_New *msg)
 
     EnterFunc(bug("VideoCoreGfx::New()\n"));
 
+    /*
+     * Retire whatever was driving this display before touching it.
+     *
+     * graphics.library offers the handover interface here and only here, in
+     * New(), where it is holding the display database on our behalf -- so it
+     * must be used now and never stashed. Without this a DDRV_BootMode driver
+     * that was serving the firmware's framebuffer stays registered and keeps
+     * refreshing into it while this driver programs its own mode over the top:
+     * two owners of one display, which showed up as the desktop drawn twice
+     * and the boot splash smeared across a framebuffer of the new width.
+     *
+     * No ranges are passed. They exist so that a boot driver serving a second,
+     * unrelated card survives, and there is one display on this machine;
+     * a NULL range list means "assume it conflicts", which is the truth here.
+     */
+    {
+        struct DisplayHandover *handover = (struct DisplayHandover *)
+            GetTagData(DDRVA_Handover, 0, msg->attrList);
+
+        if (handover)
+        {
+            APTR handle;
+            ULONG retired = 0;
+
+            while ((handle = handover->dho_FindDisplay(handover->dho_Context,
+                                                       NULL)) != NULL)
+            {
+                if (!handover->dho_ExpungeDisplay(handover->dho_Context, handle))
+                {
+                    bug("[VideoCoreGfx] boot display 0x%p still in use, cannot "
+                        "take the hardware\n", handle);
+                    return NULL;
+                }
+                retired++;
+            }
+
+            bug("[VideoCoreGfx] handover: %lu boot display(s) retired\n",
+                (unsigned long)retired);
+        }
+        else
+            bug("[VideoCoreGfx] handover: not offered, boot drivers left alone\n");
+    }
+
     NewList(&vc_modelist);
 
     FNAME_SUPPORT(SDTV_SyncGen)(&vc_modelist, cl);
